<title>USA: Mitchell Energy to sell Galveston resorts.</title>
<headline>Mitchell Energy to sell Galveston resorts.</headline>
<dateline>THE WOODLANDS, Texas 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitchell Energy &amp; Development Corp said it plans to sell its resort properties on Galveston Island as part of its real estate business restructuring.</p>
<p>The company did not say how much the properties were worth.</p>
<p>Mitchell said the properties include nearly 900 acres of undeveloped land on the west end of the island and 300 remaining lots in the Laffite's Cove, Pirate's Beach and Indian Beach residential developments, along with a small commercial center and marina.</p>
</text>
